    "final_message": "The acceptance test now passes. `scripts/verify story-drafting` is green: tessercheck zero findings, `mypy --strict` clean over 62 files, and 63 pytest tests passing against the Restate server on 38080/39070. The acceptance test file is unchanged from the red commit. Everything is committed on the branch as `8b41cda`; nothing was pushed and no PR was opened.\n\n**What it does**\n- `draft_stories` checks the job isn't blank, gets a new drafting id, saves the drafting at step `\"drafting\"`, and starts the `DraftingOrchestrator` workflow on Restate.\n- The workflow then does three steps:\n  1. Writes the stories through a `StoryWriter` port.\n  2. Saves them with the step at `\"awaiting_pick\"` and no story accepted.\n  3. Waits on the `pick_story` durable promise.\n- `get_drafting` reads the saved drafting back, or raises `DraftingNotFound`.\n- The only drafter is a deterministic one. The component refuses any other value of `STORY_DRAFTING_DRAFTER`.\n\n**Decisions to review**\n- **A new required environment variable, `STORY_DRAFTING_STORAGE`.** CI gives this tree only Restate, no Postgres, and the test process has to read what the Restate host process wrote. So draftings are stored as JSON files (atomic writes) in a directory that both processes point at. The verify arm passes the same directory to the host and to pytest, using a temp directory by default. `app/app.py` and `app/test_app.py` now read it.\n- **Scope.**\n  - Nothing yet resolves the `pick_story` promise, so a run waits there until the pick story is built.\n  - There is no real language-model writer yet.\n  - No revising and no `SKILL.md`.\n- **Verify arm.** It now serves and registers the Restate endpoint before pytest, on port 9087. It also fails if the host process has died after registration.\n\n**Something outside this worktree**\nPort 9086, the obvious next port, is held by an old `srv.restate.main` from `~/workspace/vero/go-ddd/.claude/worktrees/migrate-new-kinds` (PID 75035, running since Thursday). My first"
